"""
Writes arrays into netCDF files and reads them back, through the netCDF-C library of the system.

- Files are written in the format of netCDF 4; a variable of Float64 is NC_DOUBLE, one of Int64 NC_INT64.
- The dimensions of a variable x are named x_0, x_1 and so on, one for each axis.
- A variable is read only as the type it holds: an NC_INT64 variable is no Float64 array and the reverse.
- Every failure of the library and a missing variable come back as a fault.
- The lengths of the dimensions of a variable are checked before the array is made: a dimension of 0, and a count of elements that does not fit an Index or goes above readElementLimit(), come back as BadDimensions.  A dimension of 0 gives no empty result, since an array of this package holds every dimension at least 1, so a variable with such dimensions has no shape an array can have; the fault names the file, not the reader.
- A path or a name with a zero byte is refused by a contract, since the library would read it as ended there.

    let written: Either[NetCdfFault, Unit] := writeFloat64("out.nc", "x", &array, true);
"""
import Mirco.Array (NdArray);
import Mirco.Bindings.NetCdf (zeroFree);

module Mirco.NetCdf is
    """
    Why a call refused or failed.
    """
    union NetCdfFault: Free is
        """
        The file could not be created or opened.
        """
        case NotOpened;
        """
        The file has no variable of that name, or it could not be defined.
        """
        case NoVariable;
        """
        The variable holds elements of another type than the one asked for.
        """
        case OtherType;
        """
        The dimensions of the variable are not ones an array can have: its rank is 0 or above 32,
        a length does not fit an Index or is 0, or the count of its elements goes above
        readElementLimit().
        """
        case BadDimensions;
        """
        The library failed to write or to read the elements, or to close the file.
        """
        case NotDone;
    end;

    """
    The most elements one read of a variable makes.  A read holds the product of the lengths of
    the dimensions at or below it while it forms the product, so that the product neither
    overflows an Index nor asks for a stretch of memory no array read in one piece needs; a
    variable that announces more is refused as BadDimensions.  4294967296 elements of 8 bytes are
    32 gigabyte.
    """
    function readElementLimit(): Index
        ensures result = 4294967296;

    """
    Writes array as the variable name of the file at path: into a new file when fresh holds, which
    replaces one that is there, else into the file that is there.
    Neither path nor name holds a zero byte, which would end it for the C library.
    """
    generic [R: Region, S: Region, Q: Region]
    function writeFloat64(path: Span[Nat8, R], name: Span[Nat8, S], array: &[NdArray[Float64], Q], fresh: Bool): Either[NetCdfFault, Unit]
        requires (zeroFree(path)) and (zeroFree(name));

    """
    writeFloat64 for an array of Int64.
    """
    generic [R: Region, S: Region, Q: Region]
    function writeInt64(path: Span[Nat8, R], name: Span[Nat8, S], array: &[NdArray[Int64], Q], fresh: Bool): Either[NetCdfFault, Unit]
        requires (zeroFree(path)) and (zeroFree(name));

    """
    The variable name of the file at path as an array of Float64 with its dimensions; OtherType when it
    is not of NC_DOUBLE, BadDimensions when a length of its dimensions is 0 or the count of its
    elements does not fit an Index or goes above readElementLimit().
    """
    generic [R: Region, S: Region]
    function readFloat64(path: Span[Nat8, R], name: Span[Nat8, S]): Either[NetCdfFault, NdArray[Float64]]
        requires (zeroFree(path)) and (zeroFree(name));

    """
    The variable name of the file at path as an array of Int64; OtherType when it is not of NC_INT64,
    BadDimensions when a length of its dimensions is 0 or the count of its elements does not fit an
    Index or goes above readElementLimit().
    """
    generic [R: Region, S: Region]
    function readInt64(path: Span[Nat8, R], name: Span[Nat8, S]): Either[NetCdfFault, NdArray[Int64]]
        requires (zeroFree(path)) and (zeroFree(name));
end module.
